; The guard: the build gives an error if caravan, caravan.client or
; caravan.websocket depends on unix, on threads or on a world of weft. Thus
; the three libraries run in each world. weft.linux and weft.kqueue depend on
; weft.posix, thus the forbidden weft.posix also forbids these two worlds.
; -linkall links each module of the three libraries, thus a module that no
; other module uses also gets the check. nounix.ml is empty. The windtrap
; suites link unix, thus the guard is a separate executable with no test
; library.

(test
 (name nounix)
 (libraries caravan caravan.client caravan.websocket)
 (link_flags (-linkall))
 (forbidden_libraries unix threads.posix weft.posix weft.sim))
